00:24:38.190 --> 00:24:39.490
We should stop traffic!

00:24:40.380 --> 00:24:40.920
I'll sue!

00:24:41.300 --> 00:24:42.720
Kids, what are you gonna do?

00:24:43.080 --> 00:24:43.800
Forget it.

00:24:44.060 --> 00:24:46.300
Look, you gotta take a little less for the pig.

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:47.300
She flunked owls.

00:24:47.860 --> 00:24:49.960
The best we can do is 200 smackers.

00:24:51.050 --> 00:24:51.910
Cash money?

00:24:52.050 --> 00:24:52.370
Cash.

00:24:53.120 --> 00:24:53.540
Sold.

00:24:55.990 --> 00:24:59.150
I'm not throwing in a crown, not even a collar.

00:24:59.490 --> 00:24:59.970
To rich...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.640
Hurry, get the money.

00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:03.000
If you say so, Pop.

00:25:03.340 --> 00:25:05.140
Hold on. It's a swindle.

00:25:05.320 --> 00:25:06.780
Are you trying to ruin my career?

00:25:07.180 --> 00:25:10.220
Miss Grungy was cueing the pig to squeal at the answers.

00:25:10.680 --> 00:25:13.480
Who is this impertinent child?

00:25:13.820 --> 00:25:15.500
Bloodhound Detective Agency.

00:25:20.420 --> 00:25:21.960
Rosie was bugged.

00:25:26.810 --> 00:25:27.410
Look.

00:25:28.110 --> 00:25:29.270
A microphone.

00:25:31.050 --> 00:25:36.630
It picked up our voices, and a transmitter broadcast our questions to Miss Grungy in her truck.

00:25:37.040 --> 00:25:40.720
All she had to do was listen in on her so-called hearing aid.

00:25:41.080 --> 00:25:46.570
Don't fiddle, faddle, little Miss Bloodhound, palm that in there to fame me.

00:25:47.270 --> 00:25:52.390
When that receiver dropped out of your left ear, I noticed you didn't put it back in the same ear.

00:25:52.640 --> 00:25:53.660
You forgot yourself.

00:25:53.760 --> 00:25:58.090
I figured you might not really be hard of hearing, just pretending.

00:25:58.960 --> 00:25:59.980
That isn't a hearing aid.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:03.060
It's a device for listening to our questions from the truck.

00:26:03.200 --> 00:26:05.740
But the pig answered the questions.

00:26:06.310 --> 00:26:08.510
You'd squeal, too, if you were wearing that collar.

00:26:09.030 --> 00:26:10.650
It's a training collar for dogs.

00:26:10.790 --> 00:26:12.490
It gives very small shocks.

00:26:12.930 --> 00:26:14.050
Remote control.

00:26:14.780 --> 00:26:17.500
All Miss Grinchy had to do was press a button on her transmitter.

00:26:17.760 --> 00:26:20.600
There's a receiver built into the collar that picks up the signal

00:26:20.600 --> 00:26:22.460
and switches on the electric shock.

00:26:23.120 --> 00:26:24.960
That collar's loaded with electronics.

00:26:25.550 --> 00:26:28.840
I don't have to sign for this bad-mouthing.

00:26:40.620 --> 00:26:41.960
Didn't know you were back in town?

00:26:42.140 --> 00:26:43.500
I'm clean, Anderson.

00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:48.080
Sally, you're not peddling educated pigs again, are you?

00:26:49.840 --> 00:26:51.500
I'd better take it along as evidence.

00:26:52.400 --> 00:26:53.660
Oh, dang neighbor.

00:26:54.810 --> 00:26:55.730
Does it again, huh?

00:27:11.770 --> 00:27:12.870
Deer eat plants.

00:27:13.430 --> 00:27:16.470
We're always looking for leaves and roots, especially in the winter.

00:27:17.590 --> 00:27:19.570
Wolves are on the lookout, too, for deer.

00:27:24.640 --> 00:27:27.460
Today we've been looking at how some animals get their energy

00:27:27.460 --> 00:27:29.980
by eating plants that capture solar energy.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.800
or by eating other animals that eat plants.

00:27:33.370 --> 00:27:38.070
Thanks a lot for coming by, that was really fun.

00:27:38.070 --> 00:27:38.610
Yeah, really, thanks a lot.

00:27:38.870 --> 00:27:39.210
Bye-bye now.

00:27:39.330 --> 00:27:40.190
Bye, we enjoyed it.

00:27:40.730 --> 00:27:42.660
Hey, nice.

00:27:44.150 --> 00:27:45.260
Well, could we get a kitten?

00:27:45.880 --> 00:27:47.260
You gonna change the litter box?

00:27:47.610 --> 00:27:48.860
Well, how about a puppy?

00:27:49.270 --> 00:27:50.010
You gonna walk it?

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:03.400
Well, if we can't have a real wolf, why not a werewolf?

00:28:04.540 --> 00:28:05.420
What do you think about what they eat?

00:28:05.420 --> 00:28:05.940
I know.

00:28:10.070 --> 00:28:13.670
321 Contact is a production of the Children's Television Workshop.

00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:15.880
Thank you.

00:28:21.980 --> 00:28:22.900
It's a game show.

00:28:23.290 --> 00:28:24.650
It's a geography lesson.

00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:25.990
It's a mystery.

00:28:26.580 --> 00:28:29.980
It's the search for Carmen Sandiego, and it continues to...

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:30.860
at 430.

00:28:31.560 --> 00:28:33.740
Now, stick around for Square One TV.
